            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003Ehttps://github.com/Ambertvu/Umbraco.Community.AdminOnly\n\nAnother new package!\nAdminOnly lets administrators hide document types, tabs and properties from everyone who isn\u0026#39;t an admin \u2014 without touching user groups, permissions or document type structure. Editors see only what\u0026#39;s relevant to their work; admins keep the full picture, with a \u0026#128274; indicator next to every hidden item.\n\nHeads up \u2014 this is a backoffice UX layer, not server-side authorization. Hidden items are removed from the UI, but the underlying Umbraco APIs are untouched. A determined user with developer tools can still reach hidden content.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/Ambertvu/Umbraco.Community.AdminOnly\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003ERead the original article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
